# =============================================================================
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The line that matters is the _private/ rule below. Everything else here is
# ordinary clutter; that one rule is the only thing standing between a public
# repository and a customer's internal engineering documents.
#
# _build/ and _legacy/ ARE committed, on purpose. _build/ is how anyone rebuilds
# the site, and it is clean — the sanitiser lives there but the terms it removes
# do not. _legacy/ is the pre-2026 site, which was public all along.
#
# Three independent guards, because one is not enough for an irreversible
# mistake:
#   1. this file                      — keeps _private/ out of `git add`
#   2. .git/hooks/pre-commit          — refuses the commit even if forced
#   3. _build/scripts/check-leaks.py  — fails the build if git can see it
#
# Guard 2 is not cloned with the repository. If you ever set this project up on
# another machine, reinstall it: bash _build/scripts/install-hooks.sh
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIDENTIAL — never commit. Client source documents, the sanitiser term list,
# original artwork, strategy notes, and the setup runbook.
#
# Not in version control means NOT BACKED UP. Copy this folder somewhere safe.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
_private/

# OS clutter
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Editor and tool state — machine-specific, not part of the project
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*~

# Python bytecode from the build scripts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local scratch — anything here is disposable by definition
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
